      "description": "We rebuilt the legendary grey micro composer of 1983, then gave it everything the original owners wished for: eight voices, MPE, and a couple of new dirty tricks.\n\nThe voice is the one you know: a single fat oscillator with sawtooth and pulse (manual, LFO, or envelope PWM), a three-mode sub oscillator, and a noise source, mixed and driven into a classic four-pole lowpass filter. One snappy ADSR, switchable env/gate VCA, and an LFO with triangle, square, stepped random, and noise shapes, complete with onset delay, tempo sync, and retrigger. Portamento with the proper on/auto/off modes, and gate, gate+trig, and LFO trigger modes, exactly like the hardware.\n\nThen we went further:\n\n• Eight-voice polyphony, or the original mono behavior with the flip of a switch\n• MPE support with per-note pitch bend and pressure, four aftertouch destinations (VCO mod, VCF mod, filter freq, LFO rate), and adjustable pressure smoothing\n• MTS-ESP microtonal tuning, retuned continuously while notes sound\n• SPREAD for stereo voice panning, and AGE, which drifts each voice like forty-year-old components\n• A full drive section: pre-filter saturation, filter drive, post-VCA distortion, and a tilt EQ\n• Velocity to filter and amp\n• A chicklet keyboard with latch and octave shift, playable right on the panel\n• Full preset manager with favorites and a factory bank\n• Five faceplate colors, including one for console cowboys\n• AUv3 and standalone, with an interface that fills whatever window your host hands it\n\nAD-202 works everywhere iOS makes noise: AUM, apeMatrix, Logic Pro, GarageBand, Cubasis, and any other AUv3 host, plus a standalone app with its own audio and MIDI settings.\n\nNo subscriptions. No accounts. No nonsense. Buy it once, own it forever.",
